From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 11:18:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add map-encoder stage probe; use the repo's Tap dashes
 convention

R8 found that the R7 student's map tokens are identical for the LLM grid,
the GT grid and an all-zero grid (tok_rel = 0), so the raster path is blind
at the encoder itself, not just weak at the action head. The stage probe
loads map_encoder.* from pretraining or DAgger checkpoints and reports the
relative change the grid makes after each stage, plus the spatial
tokenizer's ||W*x|| / ||b|| ratio, to locate where the signal dies and
whether the 460000 pretraining checkpoint already carried the collapse.

map_sensitivity_probe.py now passes underscores_to_dashes to the Tap
constructor like the other scripts; configure() did not take effect on the
installed Tap version.

